"""LAMP stack sample focused on Info card fields only."""

from scryr import Diagram, Info, Link, Manifest
from scryr.types import (
    Classification,
    DeploymentTarget,
    Markdown,
    MetricTool,
    ProgrammingLanguage,
    SemVer,
    Url,
    WebFramework,
)

linux_host_block = Manifest(
    name="Linux Host",
    classification=Classification.network_gateway,
    connections=[
        Manifest(name="Apache Web Server"),
        Manifest(name="PHP Application"),
        Manifest(name="MySQL Database"),
    ],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Ubuntu VM providing the operating system, firewall rules, process supervision, and local package management for the LAMP deployment.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Shared host boundary\n"
            "\n"
            "**One machine, several failure domains:** Apache, PHP, and MySQL compete for CPU, memory, disk space, and file descriptors. Use this sample to discuss which services would move to separate hosts as traffic grows.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Resource | Proposed observation | Investigate when |\n"
            "| --- | --- | --- |\n"
            "| Memory | Available memory and swap activity | PHP workers grow while database latency rises |\n"
            "| Disk | Free space and inode usage | Logs or database files expand unexpectedly |\n"
            "| Processes | Restart count and exit reason | A service repeatedly disappears |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Maintenance exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Record the running package versions and service configuration.\n"
            "   - Identify the owner of each persistent directory.\n"
            "   - Keep application uploads separate from disposable release artifacts.\n"
            "2. Rehearse a restart on an isolated copy of the stack.\n"
            "3. Verify a static page, a dynamic page, and a database-backed workflow.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "Internet -> host firewall -> Apache -> PHP -> MySQL\n"
            "                         shared CPU / memory / disk\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> These are proposed operating checks for the sample, not evidence of a hardened host.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Define a patch window and rollback owner\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise recovery after a full host restart\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - ShellCheck for script analysis\n"
            "  - shfmt for formatting\n"
            "  - Bats for shell regression tests\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `elk_stack`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `elastic_apm`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=SemVer("22.4.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.bash],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.vm, DeploymentTarget.terraform],
        owners="Platform Team",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.elk_stack,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.elastic_apm,
        ],
        docs=["https://ubuntu.com/server/docs"],
    ),
)

apache_web_block = Manifest(
    name="Apache Web Server",
    classification=Classification.public_ui,
    connections=[Manifest(name="PHP Application")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Apache HTTP Server terminates browser traffic, serves static assets, and forwards dynamic page requests to the PHP application runtime.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Request routing and edge behavior\n"
            "\n"
            "The web server is the first application-visible hop. For this example, distinguish **static delivery** from requests that need PHP so a slow database does not look like a failure of every asset.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Request example | Intended destination | Review concern |\n"
            "| --- | --- | --- |\n"
            "| `/assets/site.css` | Static document root | Cache policy and content type |\n"
            "| `/account` | PHP application | Session handling and response time |\n"
            "| `/missing-page` | Error handler | Consistent status code and useful error page |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Suggested routing exercise\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Follow a request from the virtual host to its handler.\n"
            "   - Check the host name and document root.\n"
            "   - Identify which paths invoke PHP and which are served directly.\n"
            "2. Compare access-log timing with the corresponding application log.\n"
            "3. Recheck routing after a configuration reload.\n"
            "\n"
            "```http\n"
            "GET /assets/site.css HTTP/1.1\n"
            "Host: lamp.example.com\n"
            "Accept: text/css\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> The request is illustrative; `lamp.example.com` is a placeholder, not a running service.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Verify redirects preserve the intended path\n"
            "- [ ] Check that application source and configuration files cannot be downloaded\n"
            "- [ ] Document upload-size and timeout decisions\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Container logs for process diagnostics\n"
            "  - Resource metrics for capacity review\n"
            "  - Versioned configuration for repeatable environments\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `elk_stack`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `elastic_apm`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=SemVer("2.4.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.html],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.vm, DeploymentTarget.terraform],
        owners="Web Team",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.elk_stack,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.elastic_apm,
        ],
        docs=["https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/"],
        links=[Link(site_name="Example Site", http_url=Url("https://lamp.example.com"))],
    ),
)

php_app_block = Manifest(
    name="PHP Application",
    classification=Classification.internal_api,
    connections=[Manifest(name="MySQL Database")],
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "PHP application layer rendering server-side pages, handling form submissions, and coordinating reads and writes against MySQL.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Application responsibilities\n"
            "\n"
            "This layer turns browser actions into **validated business operations**. In a sample account workflow, it reads the session, checks permissions, validates submitted fields, and saves the resulting change through MySQL.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Workflow | Example input | Review question |\n"
            "| --- | --- | --- |\n"
            "| Sign in | Credentials and session cookie | How are failures presented without leaking account details? |\n"
            "| Edit content | Form fields and record ID | Is authorization checked for this specific record? |\n"
            "| Submit order | Item IDs and quantities | Can a duplicate submission create duplicate work? |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Walk through a write\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Validate the request before opening a database transaction.\n"
            "   - Reject unsupported values with a useful field error.\n"
            "   - Preserve safe form values so the user can correct a mistake.\n"
            "2. Commit related database changes together.\n"
            "3. Render or redirect to a result that can be safely refreshed.\n"
            "\n"
            "```text\n"
            "form -> validation -> authorization -> transaction -> response\n"
            "                         |                 |\n"
            "                    denied action      rollback on error\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> This is a design walkthrough, not a claim that every control is implemented in the sample.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Exercise expired sessions and invalid forms\n"
            "- [ ] Verify errors omit database credentials and stack traces\n"
            "- [ ] Rehearse a compatible schema migration with the Data Team\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - `laravel`\n"
            "  - `symfony`\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - Composer for dependencies\n"
            "  - PHPUnit for application tests\n"
            "  - PHPStan for static analysis\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `elk_stack`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `elastic_apm`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=SemVer("8.3.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.php],
        frameworks=[WebFramework.laravel, WebFramework.symfony],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.vm, DeploymentTarget.terraform],
        owners="App Team",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.elk_stack,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.elastic_apm,
        ],
        docs=["https://www.php.net/manual/en/", "https://laravel.com/docs"],
    ),
)

mysql_database_block = Manifest(
    name="MySQL Database",
    classification=Classification.database,
    info=Info(
        description=Markdown(
            "Relational datastore for users, sessions, application content, and transactional records used by the PHP application.\n"
            "\n"
            "### Data ownership and recovery\n"
            "\n"
            "Treat the database as the **durable boundary** of this example. Application releases may be replaced; user records and transactional history need an explicit recovery plan.\n"
            "\n"
            "| Example data | Typical access | Design consideration |\n"
            "| --- | --- | --- |\n"
            "| Users | Lookup by stable identifier | Unique constraints and access control |\n"
            "| Sessions | Lookup and expiry | Retention and cleanup |\n"
            "| Content | Filter, paginate, update | Indexes aligned with actual queries |\n"
            "| Transactions | Insert and audit by date | Atomic writes and immutable identifiers |\n"
            "\n"
            "#### Suggested recovery drill\n"
            "\n"
            "1. Restore a backup into a separate test database.\n"
            "   - Record the backup timestamp and expected data gap.\n"
            "   - Compare representative row counts and referential relationships.\n"
            "2. Point an isolated application instance at the restored database.\n"
            "3. Run a read and a rolled-back write before declaring the drill complete.\n"
            "\n"
            "```sql\n"
            "-- Illustrative read-only investigation; adapt table names to your schema.\n"
            "SELECT table_name, table_rows\n"
            "FROM information_schema.tables\n"
            "WHERE table_schema = DATABASE();\n"
            "```\n"
            "\n"
            "> Estimated table counts are diagnostic hints, not proof that a backup is complete.\n"
            "\n"
            "- [ ] Define recovery time and data-loss objectives\n"
            "- [ ] Review slow queries before adding indexes\n"
            "- [ ] Test migration rollback and restore procedures separately\n"
            "\n"
            "### Frameworks and tools\n"
            "\n"
            "- **Framework layers in this sample**\n"
            "  - No web framework is modeled for this component; inspect its service runtime and integration clients instead.\n"
            "- **Example development and investigation toolkit**\n"
            "  - SQL clients for read-only inspection\n"
            "  - Query plans for index review\n"
            "  - Migration tooling for schema changes\n"
            "- **Example observability tools**\n"
            "  - `prometheus`\n"
            "  - `elk_stack`\n"
            "  - `grafana`\n"
            "  - `elastic_apm`\n"
            "\n"
            "The tool lists illustrate a possible setup for this architecture; they do not install tools or assert that an upstream project uses every listed tool.\n"
        ),
        version=SemVer("8.4.0"),
        languages=[ProgrammingLanguage.sql],
        deployments=[DeploymentTarget.vm, DeploymentTarget.terraform],
        owners="Data Team",
        metric_tools=[
            MetricTool.prometheus,
            MetricTool.elk_stack,
            MetricTool.grafana,
            MetricTool.elastic_apm,
        ],
        docs=["https://dev.mysql.com/doc/"],
    ),
)

lamp_diagram = Diagram(
    name="LAMP",
    manifests=[
        linux_host_block,
        apache_web_block,
        php_app_block,
        mysql_database_block,
    ],
)
